From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kant <283011337+muradkant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:39:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Capture with ext-image-copy-capture where available

For damage-driven DMA-BUF capture of a whole output, use an
ext-image-copy-capture session when the compositor offers one, and fall
back to wlr-screencopy otherwise.

A pending wlr-screencopy frame makes Hyprland redraw the output at the
full refresh rate even when nothing on it changes, so damage tracking
saved nothing there; its ext-image-copy-capture frames complete only
when the output does change. The session also announces the buffer
constraints once instead of with every frame. Frames are timestamped
with the presentation time the compositor reports.

Requires wayland-protocols 1.37 at build time; older builds keep only
wlr-screencopy.
---
